-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Arms): Tactical Mastery -- parry <-> crit
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Tactical Mastery (2, 1): Redesigned. Parrying an attack grants you
--           3/6/10% critical strike chance for 10 seconds. Landing a critical
--           strike grants you 3/6/10% parry chance for 10 seconds. (3 ranks)"
--
-- Note this destroys two stock behaviours that TODO.md does not mention: the
-- rage retained on a stance change (effect 1's DUMMY, read by core's stance
-- code) and the Defensive Stance threat bonus on Bloodthirst and Mortal Strike
-- (effects 2 and 3).  All three slots are needed for the redesign.
--
-- Prior art: Turn the Tables (51627 -> 52914) is the stock "parry grants crit"
-- talent, and Blade Warding (64440) is the stock "parry grants parry".  Both
-- are aura 42 plus a spell_proc HitMask, which is the shape used here.
--
-- Spells:
--   12295 / 12676 / 12677    = Tactical Mastery ranks 1-3 (the talent)
--   200610 / 200611 / 200612 = Counterpoise, 3/6/10% crit, 10 sec
--   200613 / 200614 / 200615 = Guard Up,     3/6/10% parry, 10 sec
-- ============================================================

-- ============================================================
-- 200610-200615: the two buffs
-- ============================================================
-- Both cloned from Deflection rank 1 (16462), which is SpellFamilyName 0 with
-- no class masks or misc values -- nothing to scrub, unlike cloning the rogue
-- spell that inspired the design.
--
-- Counterpoise uses SPELL_AURA_MOD_CRIT_PCT (290), the Combat Expertise aura,
-- rather than MOD_WEAPON_CRIT_PERCENT (52).  290 feeds PLAYER_CRIT_PERCENTAGE
-- through Player::UpdateCritPercentage, which is both what melee crit rolls
-- read (Unit.cpp:3920) and what the Two-Handed Weapon Specialization conversion
-- reads.  52 is per-weapon-slot and would not.
--
-- Attributes 0: these are visible buffs, not passives.  DurationIndex 1 = 10000 ms.
-- Base points 2/5/9 render 3/6/10 under the N-1 convention.
-- SpellToolTip0 is set as well as SpellDescription0 -- the buff bar renders the
-- tooltip, and these are the two auras a player will actually watch.

DELETE FROM `alonecraft_spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (200610, 200611, 200612, 200613, 200614, 200615);
